      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "perf(mapper): cache full-root filesystem scans across concurrent mappers",
        "body": "## Description\r\nThis PR addresses a significant performance bottleneck during the initial feature mapping phase. Previously, the Go, C/C++, and Dotnet mappers unconditionally ran full-root walk() scans in parallel. In large polyglot monorepos, this resulted in 3x redundant disk I/O (redundant readdir and lstat syscalls) because these ecosystems support mapping loose source files without root-level configuration files.\r\n\r\n## Changes Made\r\nVFS Cache Module: Created src/mappers/vfs-cache.ts to memoize readdir, lstat, and realpath filesystem operations using Promises.\r\nMapperContext Update: Injected the VFS cache into the orchestrator's MapperContext so it lives for the duration of a single mapFeatures run.\r\nwalk Helper: Updated the shared walk() function in shared.ts to optionally accept and use the VFS cache for all underlying I/O.\r\nMapper Integration: Updated go.ts, c-cpp.ts, and dotnet.ts to pass the context.vfs down to their full-root traversals.\r\n\r\n## Impact\r\nConcurrent mappers hitting the same directories now share the exact same I/O operation (the first mapper pays the disk cost, and subsequent mappers instantly receive the cached memory representation). This results in a ~66% reduction in filesystem syscalls during initialization. Language-specific filters (e.g., shouldSkipCOrCppPath) continue to function identically on the cached arrays.\r\n\r\n\r\n- Fixes #158",
        "branch": "perf/shared-vfs-cache",
